  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Samsung Odyssey + when using the default bindings (as suggested after the update) this corrects the jump function, but causes the right stick forwarded to occasionally 'stick' causing you to walk into walls and objects and other players.  I have found a temporary work around, using an older community binding and remapping the Dpad to the 'right A button' which seems to allow the jump function, while still maintaining proper movement controls and gestures.  (see screenshots)  This is by no means perfect, but is a work around for now.  Hoping this can be incorporated as a fix for the default bindings for other users.  Talking to others using a 'Dell' branded headset, they were having similar issues with their stick for rotating, and know two other Samsung Odyssey Plus users, having the same issue I was expereincing.",
